                <invention-title lang="de">LINEARANTRIEB MIT UMGESTÜLPTEM KUGELGEWINDETRIEB</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">ACTIONNEUR LINÉAIRE À ENTRAÎNEMENT À VIS À BILLES RETOURNÉ</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">LINEAR ACTUATOR WITH EVERTED BALL SCREW DRIVE</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A linear actuator assembly comprising a housing, a motor, and a connecting rod. The linear actuator assembly comprises: a hollow screw shaft, defining an internal thread; a ball cylinder, comprising an external thread that is sized and shaped to oppose the internal thread. The ball cylinder comprises: a scoop insert, defining a first internal return path therethrough, a lash reduction assembly and a lash reduction spring, wherein the lash reduction spring is oriented to urge the scoop insert toward the substantially continuous working pathway; wherein the motor is configured to rotate the hollow screw shaft, thereby driving the plurality of balls along the substantially continuous ball circulation pathway, and thereby imparting linear motion to the ball cylinder.</p>
            </abstract>
